msgid "Reflection-free Jackson serialization and deserialization"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Jackson uses reflection to convert objects to and from JSON.\n"
"However, {project-name} follows a build-time optimization philosophy.\n"
"To align with this approach, configure your application to minimize "
"reflection by using the link:https://quarkus.io/extensions/io.quarkus/"
"quarkus-rest-jackson[`quarkus-rest-jackson`] extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature is introduced as a Technology Preview and is disabled by "
"default."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By eliminating reliance on reflection during deserialization, applications "
"can achieve better performance and reduced memory consumption, particularly "
"for native applications where reflection can introduce overhead.\n"
"If you implement this feature, run tests to assess its effect on your "
"applications."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable this feature, set the <<quarkus-rest-jackson_quarkus-rest-jackson-"
"optimization-enable-reflection-free-serializers,`quarkus.rest.jackson."
"optimization.enable-reflection-free-serializers`>> configuration property to "
"`true`:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus.rest.jackson.optimization.enable-reflection-free-serializers=true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Setting this property applies reflection-free optimization to "
"deserialization and serialization."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When enabled, {project-name} generates `StdSerializer` and `StdDeserializer` "
"implementations at build time for each class requiring JSON conversion. The "
"application then processes objects returned by REST endpoints using these "
"generated serializers and deserializers, eliminating reliance on reflection "
"and improving performance."
msgstr ""

