msgid "Request or response filters"
msgstr ""

msgid "Via annotations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can declare functions that are invoked in the following phases of the "
"request processing:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Before the endpoint method is identified: pre-matching request filter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After routing, but before the endpoint method is called: normal request "
"filter"
msgstr ""

msgid "After the endpoint method is called: response filter"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"These filters allow you to do various things such as examine the request "
"URI,\n"
"HTTP method, influence routing, look or change request headers, abort the "
"request,\n"
"or modify the response."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Request filters can be declared with the\n"
"link:{resteasy-reactive-api}/org/jboss/resteasy/reactive/server/"
"ServerRequestFilter.html[`@ServerRequestFilter`]\n"
"annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Request filters are usually executed on the same thread that the method that "
"handles the request will be executed.\n"
"That means that if the method servicing the request is annotated with "
"`@Blocking`, then the filters will also be run\n"
"on the worker thread.\n"
"If the method is annotated with `@NonBlocking` (or is not annotated at all), "
"then the filters will also be run\n"
"on the same event-loop thread."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If however a filter needs to be run on the event-loop despite the fact that "
"the method servicing the request will be\n"
"run on a worker thread, then `@ServerRequestFilter(nonBlocking=true)` can be "
"used.\n"
"Note however, that these filters need to be run before **any** filter that "
"does not use that setting and would run on a worker thread."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keep in mind however that the information above does **not** apply to pre-"
"matching filters (`@ServerRequestFilter(preMatching = true)`).\n"
"These filters are *always* run on an event-loop thread."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Similarly, response filters can be declared with the\n"
"link:{resteasy-reactive-api}/org/jboss/resteasy/reactive/server/"
"ServerResponseFilter.html[`@ServerResponseFilter`]\n"
"annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Such a response filter will also be called for <<exception-mapping, "
"handled>> exceptions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your filters may declare any of the following parameter types:"
